<section class="shell band">
  <div class="split">
    <div>
      <h2>Why secondary trauma, for an ethics hour</h2>
      <p>Ethics continuing education is often taught as a tour of the rules: boundaries, record
      keeping, dual relationships, the things you already know and will be reminded of once
      every two years. That version is survivable and forgettable.</p>
      <p>Secondary trauma gets at the part of ethics that actually goes wrong in practice.
      Competence is an ethical obligation, and competence degrades when a clinician is depleted
      in ways they have stopped noticing. Most ethical failures in this field are not decisions
      made badly; they are attention that was no longer there.</p>
      <p>So the session looks at what accumulates across a caseload, how it shows up before you
      can name it, what the obligation to monitor your own fitness to practice means
      concretely, and when it requires you to do something about it.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Walking it, rather than sitting through it</h3>
      {% bandArt "/assets/img/horse-grazing.jpg", 480, 640, "A horse grazing in a paddock near Dripping Springs, Texas.", "inset" %}
      <p>The two-CEU version is held outdoors, walking, among horses. That is not a gimmick
      attached to the content; it is the content. A room full of therapists discussing
      depletion while sitting still for two hours is its own small joke. Walking changes what
      people say, and horses respond to the state of the person in front of them rather than
      the credential.</p>
      <p>It also means you leave having practiced the thing rather than having heard about it.</p>
      <h3>Who it is for</h3>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li>Texas LPCs filling the 6 required ethics hours per renewal period</li>
        <li>LPC Associates, who need the same hours</li>
        <li>Clinicians who suspect they are running on empty and would rather find out on
        purpose</li>
      </ul>
      <p><a href="/texas-lpc-licensure/">What Texas requires at renewal</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

